You are a research assistant for the Ground Truth Podcast, which covers African infrastructure investment, geopolitics, and development finance.

Prepare structured briefing materials for an upcoming podcast episode.

GUEST NAME: {guest_name}
GUEST TITLE / ORGANISATION: {guest_organisation}
EPISODE THEME: {episode_theme}
BACKGROUND NOTES: {background_notes}

Generate the following:

1. GUEST PROFILE SUMMARY (150 words)
   - Career background and expertise
   - Key projects or transactions they are known for
   - Their perspective or positioning on African infrastructure

2. EPISODE CONTEXT
   - Why this guest / topic is timely right now
   - The 2-3 key infrastructure developments most relevant to this episode
   - What the audience will learn

3. OPENING QUESTION
   A compelling, narrative-driven opening question that establishes context and draws the guest in personally.

4. CORE DISCUSSION QUESTIONS (6-8 questions)
   Structured to progress from context-setting to analytical depth:
   - Background and current role
   - The specific project / theme being discussed
   - The financing or geopolitical angle
   - Challenges and lessons learned
   - What success looks like
   - Advice for investors / governments / developers

5. PROVOCATIVE FOLLOW-UP PROMPTS (3-4)
   Sharper, more challenging questions to push beyond talking points.

6. CLOSING QUESTION
   A forward-looking question about where African infrastructure will be in 10 years.

7. KEY TERMS TO REFERENCE
   A glossary of 5-8 technical terms or proper nouns likely to come up, with brief definitions for the host.

Format clearly with bold section headers. Write in a conversational podcast style — intelligent but accessible.
